From: ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T OpenBMC port
Subject: [PATCH] Legacy Mount: take a bare unix_fd, matching current bmcweb
Upstream-Status: Pending

bmcweb changed this method's prototype in commit 4bbf2a13c2 ("Virtual media
should always create pipe", Feb 2025), which now always creates the
credentials pipe and sends a bare sdbusplus::message::unix_fd -- signature
"sbh". Its commit message is explicit that this breaks downstream:

    This will break some folks downstream code, because we're changing the
    prototype here of the method call.  I try to avoid that where we can,
    but this interface isn't really viable as it is.

This daemon still registers Mount as "sbv", taking std::variant<int, unix_fd>.
sd-bus rejects the signature mismatch before the handler runs, so the only
symptom is an InsertMedia that returns "internal service error" with
`Bad D-Bus request error: Invalid argument [generic:22]` in the bmcweb log and
*nothing at all* in the virtual-media log -- the call never arrives.

Take the fd directly. Note this is the daemon catching up to a moved contract,
not a workaround for a buggy client: no released bmcweb ever sent the
variant's int arm (before 4bbf2a13c2 it sent a single-alternative
variant<unix_fd> that always held an fd), so the int arm was unreachable in
practice. sdbusplus cannot register two signatures under one method name, so
the daemon must pick one, and the one its only client sends is the right pick.

The design document in this recipe directory still describes the
VARIANT<UNIX_FD,INT> form; see the note added at the top of it.

diff --git a/src/state/initial_state.hpp b/src/state/initial_state.hpp
index f9255b0..187cec6 100644
--- a/src/state/initial_state.hpp
+++ b/src/state/initial_state.hpp
@@ -223,25 +223,21 @@ struct InitialState : public BasicStateT<InitialState>
         if (isLegacy)
         {
             using sdbusplus::message::unix_fd;
-            using optional_fd = std::variant<int, unix_fd>;
 
             iface->register_method(
                 "Mount", [&machine = machine](boost::asio::yield_context yield,
                                               std::string imgUrl, bool rw,
-                                              optional_fd fd) {
+                                              unix_fd fd) {
                     LogMsg(Logger::Info, "[App]: Mount called on ",
                            getObjectPath(machine), machine.getName());
 
                     interfaces::MountPointStateMachine::Target target = {
                         imgUrl, rw, nullptr, nullptr};
 
-                    if (std::holds_alternative<unix_fd>(fd))
                     {
-                        LogMsg(Logger::Debug, "[App] Extra data available");
-
                         // Open pipe and prepare output buffer
                         boost::asio::posix::stream_descriptor secretPipe(
-                            machine.getIoc(), dup(std::get<unix_fd>(fd).fd));
+                            machine.getIoc(), dup(fd.fd));
                         std::array<char, utils::secretLimit> buf;
 
                         // Read data
